   "stem": {
      "text": "Find the value of \\( \\lim_{h \\to 0} \\frac{(1 + h)^{2} + 3(1 + h) - 4}{h} \\)."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 5
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The numerator has the form \\( f(1 + h) - f(1) \\) with \\( f(x) = x^{2} + 3x \\), because \\( f(1) = 4 \\).",
         "mathjson": 4
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "So the function is \\( f(x) = x^{2} + 3x \\) and the base point is \\( x = 1 \\).",
         "mathjson": 1
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The limit is the definition of \\( f'(1) \\), and \\( f'(x) = 2 x + 3 \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            [
               "Multiply",
               2,
               "x"
            ],
            3
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "Evaluate: \\( f'(1) = 5 \\).",
         "mathjson": 5
      }
   ],
